  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 119 PM CDT TUE OCT 27 2026\n\nFair weather continues through Friday as we remain under the\ninfluence of high pressure. Temperatures will continue to run\nclose to seasonal normals. Some high-level clouds will scoot by\nat times, with a thicker/more persistent batch forecast tonight\nto ~midday Wednesday, associated with a lobe of ~300 mb moisture\ninbound from the west.\n\nMeanwhile, a broad trough/southwest flow pattern will establish\nacross the western U.S. This will send a couple impulses our way\nduring the weekend along with a sharp increase in vertical\nmoisture content. This trend will support showers and perhaps a\nfew rumbles of thunder. The GFS and a majority of its ensembles\nshow an earlier start to activity on Saturday whereas the ECMWF\nis later though a fraction of its ensembles are faster. The\nofficial forecast currently leans toward the scenario involving a\npotential faster onset of showers, so trick-or-treaters should at\nleast consider wet-weather impacts. Wet weather is likely through\nthe rest of the night, with the amount of lingering Sunday\nactivity dependent on the speed of the system.\n\nIt looks like we'll have a lull in rainy weather early in the\nwork week (next week), though forecast models show the potential\nfor a stronger and larger system coming our way midweek,\nproviding an opportunity for rainy (stormy?) weather.\n\n89^GSatterwhite",
